<title>FRANCE: U.S. top destination for 1996 Paris exports.</title>
<headline>U.S. top destination for 1996 Paris exports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States was the principal destination for exports from the Paris airports in 1996, Paris airport authority, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The principal destinations by country for ADP exports in</p>
<p>tonnes in 1996, with percentage change on 1995, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  United States	     128,635   up  2.0pct</p>
<p> 2  Japan			  32,350   down  8.7</p>
<p> 3  Hong Kong		    24,700   up    2.5</p>
<p> 4  Canada			 20,796   down 20.5</p>
<p> 5  Germany			20,388   up   23.9</p>
<p> 6  United Kingdom	     17,032   down 11.0</p>
<p> 7  United Arab Emirates     16,384   up   28.0</p>
<p> 8  Brazil			 15,637   down  3.9</p>
<p> 9  India			  14,819   up    3.3</p>
<p> 10 Mexico			 12,404   up   33.2</p>
<p> 11 French West Indies	 12,284   down  3.4</p>
<p> 12 Reunion			10,496   down  1.7</p>
<p> 13 Saudi Arabia		 10,240   down  0.9</p>
<p> 14 Italy			   9,509   up    1.5</p>
<p> 15 Egypt			   9,085   up   11.2</p>
<p> 16 Singapore		     9,053   up   20.5</p>
<p> 17 Korea			   8,042   down  0.3</p>
<p> 18 South Africa		  7,798   up    4.0</p>
<p> 19 Thailand			7,650   down  9.0</p>
<p> 20 China			   7,318   down 16.8</p>
<p> Total top 20 countries     394,620</p>
<p> Total all Air Exports	588,665   down  0.2</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
</text>
